  "body": "**Problem.** The built-in component library (#3645, merged in #4233) does not contain the `ISO30` holder entries of the holder library.\n\n`component_library::builtin_holders` parses the taper name with `ConnectionCode::parse`. `ISO30` is not a connection code, so the conversion skips each `ISO30` entry without a message.\n\nThe holder library defines `ISO30` as the router name of DIN 69871 size 30, with the same steel as `SK30` (`crates/tools/src/holder_library_din.rs`, `pub const ISO30: Taper = Taper { name: \"ISO30\", ..SK30 }`).\n\n**Effect.** A router user cannot select an `ISO30` holder from the built-in components. The user must draw the holder by hand. No wrong output: the entry is missing, not wrong.\n\n**Done means.**\n- Decide how `ISO30` maps: an alias of `SK30` in `ConnectionCode::parse`, or a separate code that mates only `ISO30`. Record the decision in `docs/decisions/`.\n- The `ISO30` entries are built-in components.\n- Remove the `ISO30` exception from the test `every_holder_with_a_taper_is_a_built_in_and_a_shrink_fit_bore_is_plain` in `crates/app/tests/tool_library_holders/builtin_shrink.rs` (PR #4251).\n\nFound during the review fix of PR #4251. The effort is `effort:high` because built-in holder outlines feed the collision checks (safety floor).\n",
